WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.234
Modern expertise is often distributed.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:06.595
A team may hold more capability than any one individual because knowledge is spread across

00:00:06.595 --> 00:00:07.000
people,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.880
documentation, tools, automation, and routines.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.865
Shared mental models help the group coordinate.

00:00:11.865 --> 00:00:15.255
Handoffs help expertise move across time and role boundaries.

00:00:15.255 --> 00:00:19.170
Documentation makes important reasoning visible instead of trapping it inside one person's

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:19.700
memory.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.540
Tools can extend expertise when they reduce routine burden, preserve context,

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.595
surface patterns, or make review easier.

00:00:25.595 --> 00:00:27.970
Automation can help with consistency and speed.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:32.800
AI assistance can summarize, draft, compare, search, classify, or generate options.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.765
But tool output still needs expert review.

00:00:34.765 --> 00:00:38.770
A tool can produce fluent results without understanding context, consequences,

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.915
or the organization's tolerance for risk.

00:00:40.915 --> 00:00:42.965
A major challenge is avoiding deskilling.

00:00:42.965 --> 00:00:45.300
If people accept tool output without inspection,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.410
they may lose the habit of checking assumptions, noticing exceptions,

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:50.400
and understanding why an answer is appropriate.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.020
Better designs keep humans engaged in the judgment loop.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.450
They use tools to make expertise more effective,

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.485
not to hide the work so completely that no one can evaluate it.

00:00:58.485 --> 00:01:02.875
Teams can make expertise reusable by capturing examples, decision records, review notes,

00:01:02.875 --> 00:01:04.615
checklists, and lessons learned.

00:01:04.615 --> 00:01:07.850
They can teach expertise by explaining how strong performers think,

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.300
not just what they conclude.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.600
AI-assisted work makes this even more important.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.510
The strongest teams use tools to amplify judgment, while preserving accountability,

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.700
review, and the ability to explain why a decision makes sense.
